Breeze: a breezerc key for the window corner radius (Mauvely OS)

Breeze rounds windows at Frame_FrameRadius (2.5) times the small spacing,
5 px on Wayland, and has no setting for it. This adds one:

  breezerc [Common] CornerRadius=<logical pixels>

Unset or negative keeps Breeze's own radius. Mauvely OS sets 8 in
/usr/share/mauvely/xdg/breezerc; the Plasma preset writes -1.

Made against Breeze 6.7.5 (plasma-breeze-6.7.5-1.fc44). os-image applies it
with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0`; HANDOFF.md says how to refresh it.

--- a/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp
+++ b/kdecoration/breezedecoration.cpp
@@ -854,7 +854,9 @@
     // On X11, the smallSpacing value is used for scaling.
     // On Wayland, this value has constant factor of 2.
     // Removing it will break radius scaling on X11.
-    m_scaledCornerRadius = KDecoration3::snapToPixelGrid(Metrics::Frame_FrameRadius * settings()->smallSpacing(), window()->nextScale());
+    // A CornerRadius in breezerc, in logical pixels, replaces it.
+    const qreal radius = m_internalSettings->cornerRadius() >= 0 ? m_internalSettings->cornerRadius() : Metrics::Frame_FrameRadius * settings()->smallSpacing();
+    m_scaledCornerRadius = KDecoration3::snapToPixelGrid(radius, window()->nextScale());
 }
 
 void Decoration::updateScale()
--- a/kdecoration/breezesettingsdata.kcfg
+++ b/kdecoration/breezesettingsdata.kcfg
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@
     <entry name="RoundedCorners" type = "Bool">
       <default>true</default>
     </entry>
+
+    <!-- window corner radius, in logical pixels; negative keeps Breeze's own (Frame_FrameRadius in units of small spacing) -->
+    <entry name="CornerRadius" type = "Double">
+      <default>-1</default>
+    </entry>
   </group>
 
   <group name="Windeco">
